# The music player's OWN authorable components (docs/ecs-systems-own-their-
# tables.md §3): lib/ui tables until the ECS split step 4 moved them next to
# the system that reads them. A `.raescene` still authors them by name; the
# loader parks a name no lib table has in `world.pendingComponents` and
# applyMusicComponents (MusicSystems.rae) decodes each into its system.
open ui/Components

# A playback time label: the M:SS position (`elapsed`) or track duration
# (`total`), read from PlaybackSystem by `playbackTimeSystem` and written to
# the node's `Text.text` whenever the whole second changes. Distinct from
# TrackText (which follows the browsed track's title / artist).
enum PlaybackTimeKind { elapsed, total }

# ----- playback widgets: the data bindings the dock and Now Playing share (#981)
# Each is authored on the node it drives; the matching system runs every frame
# from `refreshMountedUi` (and once at mount) and writes only on a change of
# its observed revision / key, so the same components serve the dock's
# mini-player and the Now Playing page.
# Play/pause glyph: the Sprite key follows `PlaybackSystem.isPlaying` and the
# WidgetState.selected flag mirrors it (`revision` observed).
type PlaybackIcon {
  builtRevision: Int = -1
}

# Now-playing cover: the Sprite key follows the playing track's art
# (`nowPlayingRevision` observed); seeded from the browsed album at mount.
# Its corner rounding is an authored `CornerRadius` like every other cover
# (the app's AlbumCoverSystem squares / restores it with the setting).
type PlaybackCover {
  builtRevision: Int = -1
}

# Heart / like button: WidgetState.selected follows the liked playlist
# membership of the browsed track; the outline/filled StateStyle is
# installed by the system (StateStyle is a runtime table).
type LikedHeart {
  styled: Bool = false
}

# Track text: `field` is "title" or "artist" (the Text follows the browsed
# album + track, `builtKey` = stem|index), or "timeNow" / "timeTotal" (the
# M:SS playback position / duration, written whenever the second changes).
type TrackText {
  field: String = "title"
  builtKey: String
}

type PlaybackTime {
  kind: PlaybackTimeKind
  builtSecond: Int = -1
}
